    para('Hausdorff here is a sampled-point-to-exact-polyline maximum. With <=10 mm query spacing, continuous Hausdorff lies between this maximum and maximum+5 mm. A 20 mm spacing repeat measures discretization sensitivity. Summary P95 and Hausdorff are equal-person means of trial statistics, not global maxima or pooled percentiles.')
    para('Observed gaps prevent honest full-trial continuous Frechet comparison. Discrete Frechet is calculated separately inside supported temporal runs at25 mm spatial spacing (50 mm convergence repeat), taking the maximum run value. This preserves ordering inside runs only. Arc-length correspondence independently normalizes paired runs by their traveled distance; it is diagnostic and never corrects a model or resets an origin.')
