    para('Two axle markers establish midpoint and axle direction, not full body pitch. Gravity does not establish absolute yaw. Camera reprojection residuals are not absolute millimeter position uncertainty. The empirical raw-to-speed coefficients absorb configured radius; changing a radius metadata field alone may leave the estimator unchanged. Full mounting/lever-arm compensation needs calibrated axes, phase and body angular motion.')
    para('Current best hypothesis: heterogeneous errors from travel/braking deficits, yaw-induced lateral accumulation, residual clock offset, pitch/mounting coupling and unresolved reference-front semantics. A calibrated wheel/body estimator with wheelchair-trained interval displacement/heading corrections and uncertainty-aware SE(2) smoothing is defensible. Large networks or RL alone do not supply missing calibration or observable absolute position.')
